.TH KEEL 1 "October 2026" "keel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keel \- HTTP/1.1 static file server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keel
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-bind
.IR address ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-\-workers
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-access\-log
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-error\-log
.IR path ]
.PP
.B keel
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
.PP
.B keel
.B \-v
|
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keel
serves files over HTTP/1.1 from a single document root.
It is intended to run on Linux.
Put TLS on a reverse proxy in front of it when clients are not on a trusted network.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B keel
listens on 0.0.0.0 port 8080 and serves the current directory.
Flags override the same settings in a config file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read
.I file
before applying flags.
The file is line oriented:
a key, then a value.
Lines starting with # are comments.
An example ships with the source as keel.conf.example.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " address"
Local address to listen on.
The default is 0.0.0.0.
An IPv6 address, including ::, is accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
TCP port.
0 selects an ephemeral port, which is printed at startup.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " directory"
Document root.
The path must be a directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " n"
Number of event-loop threads.
0, the default, uses one worker per online CPU.
.TP
.BI \-\-access\-log " path"
Combined access log.
The default is standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-error\-log " path"
Error log.
The default is standard error.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Each non-empty, non-comment line is a key and a value.
Values with spaces may be quoted.
The keys are
.BR bind ,
.BR port ,
.BR root ,
.BR workers ,
.BR max_connections ,
.BR header_timeout_ms ,
.BR keepalive_timeout_ms ,
.BR write_timeout_ms ,
.BR max_header_bytes ,
.BR max_requests_per_conn ,
.BR index ,
.BR directory_listing ,
.BR server_name ,
.BR server_header ,
.BR access_log ,
.BR error_log ,
and
.BR log_level .
.PP
.B directory_listing
is
.BR on " or " off .
It defaults to off.
.B log_level
is
.BR error ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
or
.BR debug .
.B server_name ,
when set, requires the Host header to match.
An empty
.B server_header
omits the Server response header.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop accepting, close idle connections, finish work already in progress for up to five seconds, then exit 0.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reopen the access and error logs.
The listen address and document root stay as they were at startup.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.SH FILES
A running server also recognizes
.I errors/NNN.html
under the document root as the body for HTTP status
.IR NNN .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B keel
exits 0 after a clean shutdown, 1 on a startup failure, and 2 when the command line or config file is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README in the source tree.
